          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Winston Churchill</strong><br>\nWinston Churchill was born on November 30, 1874, in Blenheim Palace, England. As a young boy, Churchill struggled in school but excelled in English and history. He came from a prestigious family; his father, Lord Randolph Churchill, was a prominent politician. Despite a distant relationship with his parents, Churchill's nanny, Elizabeth Everest, played a crucial role in his upbringing, providing the affection and support he needed.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Churchill's Military Career</strong><br>\nChurchill joined the British Army in 1895 and served in India, Sudan, and South Africa. During his military service, he wrote reports for newspapers and books about his experiences. His participation in the Battle of Omdurman and escape from a POW camp in the Second Boer War made him a national hero. These exploits also provided material for his writing career.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Entry into Politics</strong><br>\nAfter his military service, Churchill began his political career. He was first elected to Parliament in 1900 as a Conservative but switched to the Liberal Party in 1904. His early political work focused on social reforms and modernizing the British Navy. Churchill’s ability to switch parties demonstrated his commitment to his principles over party loyalty.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
