          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Role in World War I</strong><br>\nDuring World War I, Churchill served as First Lord of the Admiralty, overseeing the British Navy. He faced criticism for the Gallipoli Campaign's failure, which led to his resignation. However, he returned to government positions later in the war, serving on the Western Front and proving his resilience and dedication to public service.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Interwar Period</strong><br>\nAfter World War I, Churchill held various government positions, including Minister for the Colonies, where he helped draft the Treaty of Sevres to settle Middle Eastern borders. He also warned about the rise of Nazi Germany in the 1930s, urging Britain to strengthen its defenses against potential threats.</p>\n\n<p><strong>World War II Leadership</strong><br>\nChurchill became Prime Minister in 1940, leading Britain through World War II. His speeches inspired resistance against Nazi aggression and hope during the war's darkest days. He focused on forming alliances, notably with the United States and the Soviet Union, to defeat the Axis powers. His leadership during this period is widely celebrated.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
